# Counter-example: a gmeow:GmnSecurityRing whose authored lattice
# coordinates are malformed — it carries NO gmeow:gmnRingLevel at all, so it cannot be
# placed in the Denning product-order lattice. sh:minCount 1 on the gmeow:gmnRingLevel
# property of lang:GmnRingLatticeWellFormedShape fires shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent
# (lang:GmnRingLatticeMalformed). This gates the AUTHORED coordinate, never the derived
# gmeow:gmnRingWithin relation (gating the derived relation would be a tautology).

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/lang/> .

ex:ringMissingLevel a gmeow:GmnSecurityRing ;
    rdfs:label "ring missing its level coordinate" .
